TEXT -240 -152 Left 2 ;Normal a overheadline has Self and mutual inductances\nFor the symmetric (or loadflow) case the working inductance\nis computed as selfinductance minus mutual inductance\nThan this impedance remains unchanged! \nFor use with also asymmetric cases the line inductances are modelled with\ncoupling factors. The coupling factor remains constant but\nthe operating mode (symmetric,1phase fault) can change the\nactual working inductance of the line. \nFor symmetric operating mode both simulation results are equal.\nFor assymetric operating modes Z0 is significant\nE.g for a 1 phase earth fault in a grouded system the current \nis computed much smaller if the coupling is included (Z0 high)\nIf simulated with uncoupled line the current is much higher (Z0=Z1=lower)
